The following are tutorials intended to introduce the usage of ExaHyPE 2 to new users.
There will be a some brief touches of theory intended to explain what ExaHyPE 2 is and what design choices went into it,
but for the most part these are intended to be a practical introduction into application development in ExaHyPE 2.

Structurally, these tutorials are composed of text-based explanations, what you are currently reading, accompanied by jupyter notebooks which you can find in

       cd tutorials/exahype2

Please browse the links below and study the webpages, and where appropriate go find the accompanying jupyter notebook to see the realization in code.
Best of luck and best of fun!
</div>

